==Getting Started==

If you wish to make non-metal armor for yourself and others, tailoring is the skill you need to learn. The first thing you will need is access to either; [[Small Sewing Kit]], [[Large Sewing Kit]], [[Deluxe Sewing Kit]], or [[Loom]]; additionally there is a [[Coldain Tanners Kit]] for higher level [[Velious]] tailoring.  Your first finished products will be [[Patchwork Armor]] for the non-casters, and [[Silk Swatch]]es and [[Raw Silk Armor]] for the pure spellcasters and [[Monk]]s. Although, if you are interested in the best way to raise your skill check out the [[Skill Tailoring#Leveling Guide|Leveling Guide]].  

''' Pelts and Skins '''

[[Verant]] was somewhat inconsistent in the way hides are named.  For the most part they are interchangeable terms - if you have a "skin", but a recipe calls for a "pelt" it should work.  Wolf, cat and bear pelts drop from various animals scattered all over Norrath. They come in a variety of different standard qualities; High, Medium, Low, and Ruined Quality. Additionally there are 'superb' and 'excellent' quality skins used in cultural tailoring.  The major difference between wolf, cat and bear pelts is the size of the armor they create; Wolf-Small, Cat-Medium, Bear-Large.

''' Velious '''

Items for all of the [[Velious]] recipes may be obtained with varying levels of difficulty from across Velious zones. If you are having a tailor make something for you, please have mercy on them and help them gather the difficult stuff first; which may be the pelts, oils, or Velium ore depending on the combine as to which pieces are the most difficult.

'''WARNING -''' The Coldain Shawl requires you to level tailoring to 162 and preferably to 208 so all needed combines will be trivial. Most people level to 162 versus 208 and hope their 208 combine doesn't fail. If it does fail, those ingredients are not that hard to re-acquire, which is why people are willing to take the risk.

While it was true that most people stopped at 162 - in Everquest Legends, all players can use the [[Forest Green Silk Swatch]] to get Tailoring to 190. It's a bit of a pain because it requires ground spawns from Greater Faydark, but about 6-9 of them spawn every ~5 minutes, and with jumping to other instances the items can be acquired fairly quickly. Assuming the Coldain Shawl is added to EQ Legends, its probably preferable for anyone doing the quest to get to 190 Tailoring at a minimum. (Approximately 234 combines to progress from 158-190 at 451 wisdom.)

